sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Murray (1981) Thomas substrate-inhibition reaction-diffusion pre-pattern, conical tail spot-to-ring transition & P1 surface-FEM felid body — MorphoEval overall 84.2/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 3 (v3) post-remediation evaluation of `1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py` (overall weighted score: 84.2 / 100, DOWN 7.4 points from 91.6 / 100 in Pass 2, up from 49.4 / 100 in Pass 1). The v3 script keeps the exact Thomas (1975) / Murray (1981) steady state, Jacobian, d_c and dispersion analysis; replaces the numerically unstable v2 conical-tail solver with a fully implicit surface-of-revolution Laplace-Beltrami solver (metric factor 1/(1+r'^2) included) and shows that the v2 geometry has no ring zone; adds a P1 cotangent surface finite-element solver on a triangulated 3D felid body of revolution (47,520 vertices) verified against the exact cylinder spectrum, on which the Liu, Liaw & Maini (2006) two-stage protocol is run as a genuine PDE (cub body -> adult body, growth factor G = 2) yielding torso annularity 0.84 and a tail ring onset at x/L_tail = 0.82 vs the Lean-backed prediction 0.86; sweeps G in {1, 1.5, 2, 3} on the planar flank; and backs five mathematical laws with machine-checked Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys). The score falls because v3 retracts the v2 865x suppression ratio (clipping artifact), shows the v2 \"two-stage\" step to have been an image filter on a linear-regime field, finds the specimen tail ROI mis-placed, reports a 3.7x marking-density shortfall against the specimen (5.1 vs 18.9 markings per torso depth), and finds the kinetic CLI flags unwired -- none of which v2 had penalised. Overall 84.2/100 (faithfulness 81.1, reproducibility 91.2); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 64526a0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 72, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/mammalian_coat_markings_comparison.png: rendered output of 1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py at 64526a0, image/png, 1273921 B, 2366×1881 px, artifact_sha256 417dee8b24b004962c52143eefd329402da37f468ef4c9cbd844a2d13282558a (sha256 417dee8b24b004962c52143eefd329402da37f468ef4c9cbd844a2d13282558a), spec_fingerprint b990576b2a4b3ccd36c08d1a21625f5ebd87766fc673675eaee0d8216821ffd3. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: b990576b2a4b3ccd36c08d1a21625f5ebd87766fc673675eaee0d8216821ffd3; artifact_sha256: 417dee8b24b004962c52143eefd329402da37f468ef4c9cbd844a2d13282558a; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/felid_body_profile.json=65978462afc1b9e7..., datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/mammalian_coat_markings_reference.json=24d56069831e0ee9..., datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/panthera_pardus_specimen.jpg=86533a5dcf9cfee6..., datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/scout_manifest.json=28eabc9cf247b03e...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-mammalian-coat-markings-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Murray (1981): Thomas substrate-inhibition kinetics at a = 92, b = 64, alpha = 1.5, rho = 18.5, K = 0.1 are diffusively unstable for d > d_c; the domain scale factor gamma selects between no pattern, stripes, spots and crowding; on a tapered cylinder spot modes (m >= 1) are excluded below a critical radius so a spotted animal can have a ringed tail but not vice versa | Liu, Liaw & Maini (2006): leopard rosettes arise from a two-stage process in which a juvenile spot pre-pattern is re-run under changed parameters on the grown adult skin | Dziuk (1988), Pinkall & Polthier (1993), Dziuk & Elliott (2013): P1 surface finite elements with cotangent weights converge to the Laplace-Beltrami operator on a triangulated surface; reconstructed_in_script: Exact steady state, Jacobian, d_c, dispersion curve and Turing band; Neumann cylinder eigenmode counting including n = 0; r_crit (fastest-mode) and r_excl = 1/k_+ (full-exclusion) radii; fully implicit conical-tail PDE; planar DCT-II IMEX PDE run to saturation with a genuine two-stage protocol and growth-factor sweep; P1 surface FEM (stiffness/mass assembly, spectrum verification, two-stage run on the felid body) with annularity and spot-spacing diagnostics; DoG segmentation of the Kruger specimen; transfer_boundary: The 3D body is a parametric surface of revolution with hand-set knots (felid_body_profile.json), not a photogrammetric scan; its head-body length of 22 cub wavelengths and the growth factor G = 2 are ASSUMED, not fitted, which is why the FEM marking density (5.1 per torso depth) is 3.7x below the specimen estimate (18.9) | The tail ring onset comparison (0.82 measured vs 0.86 predicted) is on the surrogate taper, whose tip radius (0.004 HBL) was chosen to lie below r_excl; it is a consistency check of solver against linear theory, not a measurement on a real tail | The specimen is a 3/4-view photograph: the flank ROI is foreshortened and the v2 tail ROI covers hindquarters/background, so the Delaunay CV and polygonality are flank-only statistics; does_not_claim: That Murray (1981) or Liu et al. (2006) reported any of the FEM, annularity, growth-sweep or marking-density numbers; all are v3 reconstructions | That the Thomas kinetics are the biological mechanism of felid pigmentation." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add the surface-FEM and body-proportion references (Dziuk 1988, Pinkall & Polthier 1993, Dziuk & Elliott 2013, Stein & Hayssen 2013) to `datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/paper_citations.bib` and re-pin its SHA-256 in `EXPECTED_SHA256` (L128-130).",
            "remediation needed: Fit the body scale and growth factor to the specimen instead of assuming them: HBL = 22 lambda_c and G = 2 give 5.09 markings per torso depth vs 18.9 observed (`run_two_stage_fem_body`, L1025-1053; measurement 'FEM Stage-2 torso markings per torso depth', L1573-1581). Sweep HBL/lambda_c in [22, 90] and G in [1.5, 3] and report the (HBL, G) that matches the specimen density and polygonality jointly.",
            "remediation needed: Make the initial noise field mesh-resolution independent (`integrate_thomas_fem_surface_pde` L870-876 draws per-vertex noise; planar reseed at L544), e.g. by projecting a fixed low-pass random field onto the mesh, so that the FEM spot layout is reproducible across `nx`/`ntheta` and the coarse self-test body (nx = 200) and the default render (nx = 360) seed the same pattern.",
            "remediation needed: Relocate the specimen tail ROI onto the curled tail (approximately x = 470-530, y = 200-240 per `felid_body_profile.json` L64) or replace the 3/4-view specimen with a lateral-view, SHA-pinned photograph in which the tail is resolved, then add a measured tail spot-to-ring onset to compare with `tail_exclusion_fraction` (currently only the surrogate-mesh value is compared, L1543-1551).",
            "remediation needed: Replace the parametric surface of revolution with a triangulated photogrammetric or CT-derived felid body mesh (`build_felid_body_surface_mesh`, L791-834; profile knots at `datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/felid_body_profile.json` L44-48): the FEM assembly (`assemble_p1_fem_laplace_beltrami`, L721-753) is already mesh-agnostic, so this is a data item, not a solver item. Carried over from v2 in reduced form.",
            "remediation needed: Wire the kinetic and scale CLI flags into the solvers: `--a`, `--b`, `--alpha`, `--rho`, `--K`, `--d`, `--gamma`, `--steps`, `--seed` are parsed at L1783-1791 but `render_outputs()` is called with `growth_factor` only (L1800); thread a parameter dict through `compute_thomas_steady_state`, `integrate_thomas_pde_2d`, `integrate_thomas_conical_tail_pde` and `run_two_stage_fem_body`, and add a self-test check that `--K 0` reproduces the negative control." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.842"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (Slot 003 autonomous loop assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

